<title>FRANCE: French consumer spending fell 0.8 pct in December.</title>
<headline>French consumer spending fell 0.8 pct in December.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-01-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>National statistics institute INSEE gave the following seasonally adjusted figures for household spending on manufactured goods in billions of 1980 francs:</p>
<p>					    Dec    Nov    Oct     Dec 1995</p>
<p> Total				   57.28  57.72   58.04     56.64</p>
<p> Total change (pct v pvs month)   -0.8   -0.5    -3.8	 N/A</p>
<p> Retail sector			 38.23  38.94   38.18     37.64</p>
<p> Durables				16.73  16.82   17.60     16.54</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   11.16  11.19   11.11     11.03</p>
<p> Other				   29.39  29.71   29.32     29.07</p>
<p>It gave the following percentage changes (month-on-month unless stated)</p>
<p>					    Dec    Nov    Oct    Dec yr/yr</p>
<p> Total				   -0.8   -0.5    -3.8	  1.1</p>
<p> Retail sector			 -1.8    2.0     1.7	  1.5</p>
<p> Durables				-0.6   -4.5   -13.5	  1.1</p>
<p>   of which cars			5.3  -18.2   -27.3	 -0.4</p>
<p>   household equip		   -3.8    5.4     0.3	  2.0</p>
<p> Textiles, leather		   -0.3    0.7     3.2	  1.2</p>
<p> Other				   -1.1    1.3     0.4	  1.1</p>
<p>NOTE - INSEE said on December 27 that consumer spending fell 0.8 percent in November. It said consumption fell 3.4 percent in the fourth quarter of 1996 after rising 2.8 percent in the third quarter.</p>
<p>-- Paris Newsroom +331 4221 5452</p>
</text>
